NOTICE
======

Secret Agent Browser MCPs is an adapted collection of MCP tools for popular stealth-automation
browsers, through the Playwright MCP contract. It is derived from swimmwatch/cloakbrowser-mcp
(MIT). The bridge, its CLI, packaging and the docs/ tree are upstream's work; this repository
adapts them into a Claude Code plugin marketplace and adds a complete, proper stealth
implementation for agentic harnesses and tasks. Full detail is in README.md.

Attribution
-----------

- Upstream bridge - swimmwatch/cloakbrowser-mcp
  https://github.com/swimmwatch/cloakbrowser-mcp
  MIT. The Playwright MCP-compatible bridge, CLI, Docker/HTTP packaging and the documentation
  carried under docs/ come from this project.

- CloakBrowser - https://github.com/CloakHQ/CloakBrowser
  The stealth-patched Chromium binary and engine wrapper used by the cloak engine. The binary is
  proprietary: the v146 build is free and current builds require a vendor licence for more than
  one concurrent session. This repository does not bundle it.

- Playwright MCP - https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-mcp
  The source of the tool names and schemas exposed through the contract. Parity is structural,
  not a reimplementation.

- Camoufox - https://github.com/camoufox-org/camoufox
  The stealth Firefox browser behind the camoufox and camoufox-native engines.

- camoufox-playwright-mcp 0.1.5 - https://pypi.org/project/camoufox-playwright-mcp/
  The pinned wrapper that drives the Camoufox engine. It is fetched from PyPI at first start into
  plugin data and is never bundled or redistributed here. No source-repository URL appears in the
  pinned artifacts, so the package page is cited instead of guessing one.

- mcp-camoufox 0.4.5 - https://pypi.org/project/mcp-camoufox/
  The native Camoufox MCP server, fetched from PyPI at first start and never bundled here. Its
  licence is FSL-1.1-MIT (source-available; not OSI-approved). The npm package of the same name is
  a different project.

- Kameleo - https://kameleo.io/downloads
  A proprietary desktop application the user installs and licenses separately. The plugin only
  attaches to its local CDP endpoint and never downloads, installs or redistributes the app. The
  attach path is live-unverified.

Derivation
----------

This repository is adapted from swimmwatch/cloakbrowser-mcp (MIT). It is a collection of adapted
MCP tools for popular stealth-automation browsers, through the Playwright MCP contract, and adds a
complete, proper stealth implementation for agentic harnesses and tasks. The marketplace, plugins
and broker are this project's work; the upstream bridge remains upstream's.

